questions.answer:
Register for courses early, and if at all possible do the "pre-enrollment" which is the earliest possible. Also, during pre-enrollment it seemed that professors were more willing to ignore prerequisites. Also, during the add-drop period, you can go to any lectures and "try them out" to see if you want to attend or no.
DO YOURSELF A FAVOUR and use UST-Space (
https://ust.space/
) (requires HKUST logon) and UST-Rankings (
https://ust-rankings.com/
) to see rankings of professors and courses you might be interested in taking, students are very good at reporting good as well as bad profs and courses. Also, most courses are offered at different times and _with different profs_. Try out different professors for a specific course during add/drop, if one('s teaching style) isn't to your liking.
